NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 "Config::INI - simple .ini-file format"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "version 0.029"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "=head1 SYNOPSIS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "Config-INI comes with code for reading F<.ini> files:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 "  my $config_hash = Config::INI::Reader->read_file('config.ini');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 "...and for writing C<.ini> files:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "  Config::INI::Writer->write_file({ somekey => 'somevalue' }, 'config.ini');"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 "See L<Config::INI::Writer> and L<Config::INI::Reader> for more examples."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 "=head1 PERL VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 "This library should run on perls released even a long time ago.  It should work"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 "on any version of perl released in the last five years."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 "Although it may work on older versions of perl, no guarantee is made that the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 "minimum required version will not be increased.  The version may be increased"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 "for any reason, and there is no promise that patches will be accepted to lower"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 "the minimum required perl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 "=head1 GRAMMAR"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "This section describes the format parsed and produced by Config::INI::Reader"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 "and ::Writer.  It is not an exhaustive and rigorously tested formal grammar,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "it's just a description of this particular implementation of the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 "not-quite-standardized \"INI\" format."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 "  ini-file   = { <section> | <empty-line> }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 "  empty-line = [ <space> ] <line-ending>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 "  section        = <section-header> { <value-assignment> | <empty-line> }"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "  section-header = [ <space> ] \"[\" <section-name> \"]\" [ <space> ] <line-ending>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 "  section-name   = string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000135 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000136 "  value-assignment = [ <space> ] <property-name> [ <space> ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000137 "                     \"=\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000138 "                     [ <space> ] <value> [ <space> ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000139 "                     <line-ending>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000140 "  property-name    = string-without-equals"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000141 "  value            = string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000142 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000143 "  comment     = <space> \";\" [ <string> ]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000144 "  line-ending = [ <comment> ] <EOL>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000145 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000146 "  space = ( <TAB> | \" \" ) *"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000147 "  string-without-equals = string - \"=\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000148 "  string = ? 1+ characters; not \";\" or EOL; begins and ends with non-space ?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000149 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000150 "Of special note is the fact that I<no> escaping mechanism is defined, meaning"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000151 "that there is no way to include an EOL or semicolon (for example) in a value,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000152 "property name, or section name.  If you need this, either subclass, wait for a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000153 "subclass to be written for you, or find one of the many other INI-style parsers"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000154 "on the CPAN."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000155 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000156 "The order of sections and value assignments within a section are not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000157 "significant, except that given multiple assignments to one property name within"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000158 "a section, only the final one is used.  A section name may be used more than"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000159 "once; this will have the identical meaning as having all property assignments"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000160 "in all sections of that name in sequence."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000161 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000162 "=head1 DON'T FORGET"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000163 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000164 "The definitions above refer to the format used by the Reader and Writer classes"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000165 "bundled in the Config-INI distribution.  These classes are designed for easy"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000166 "subclassing, so it should be easy to replace their behavior with whatever"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000167 "behavior your want."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000169 "Patches, feature requests, and bug reports are welcome -- but I'm more"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000170 "interested in making sure you can write a subclass that does what you need, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000171 "less in making Config-INI do what you want directly."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000173 "=head1 THANKS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000175 "Thanks to Florian Ragwitz for improving the subclassability of Config-INI's"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000176 "modules, and for helping me do some of my first merging with git(7)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000177 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000178 "=head1 ORIGIN"
